<body>
{{> cabecera_en 1=k}}
<main class="guia-log blog-learn" id="inicio">
<article>
<section class="portada solo">
<div class="envoltura">
<div>
<h1>Learn MTG Arena with Guides Inside ManaLab 3.0</h1>
<p class="autoria"><time datetime="{{FECHA_BLOG_LEARN}}">{{FECHA_BLOG_LEARN:texto}}</time> · ManaLab</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="seccion">
<div class="envoltura">
<div class="cuerpo-blog">
<p>You finish a session and open your stats. One row stands out: you keep losing to the same deck. The tracker has told you <em>where</em> you lose. It can't tell you <em>how to fix it</em>.</p>
<p>ManaLab 3.0 adds a section for that next step. It's called <strong>Learn</strong>.</p>
<h2>From "I lose to this deck" to "here's how to beat it"</h2>
<p>ManaLab has always been about knowing what actually happens in your games: your opening hands, your mulligans, your results against each deck. That data is only useful if you do something with it.</p>
<p>Learn sits in the same app, one click from your stats. When your numbers point at a weak spot, the study material is already there. No tab-hopping, no searching for a guide you half remember.</p>
<h2>What's inside Learn</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Magic guides from Metafy creators</strong>, for Arena and Magic Online. The list refreshes on its own, so new guides show up without you updating anything.</li>
<li><strong>Featured creators</strong>, marked with a visible label.</li>
<li><strong>Coaching sessions</strong> with featured creators, if you'd rather have a person look at your play than read about it.</li>
<li><strong>Cover art loaded from Metafy.</strong> What you see is what the creator published.</li>
</ul>
<!-- CAPTURA-LEARN: pendiente (pantalla Aprender 3.0, datos de ejemplo, sin rivales; alt ≤125) -->
<h2>How featured creators are chosen</h2>
<p>You should know why a creator is highlighted. Creators appear as featured in ManaLab through a Featured Creator membership on Metafy, and the app marks them with a label. It's a paid placement on the creator's side, not a ranking of who is best. Read the guide, check the creator, decide.</p>
<h2>The tracker is still free</h2>
<p>ManaLab itself stays free to download and use. The only paid piece is the optional AI analysis of your losses, a separate membership on Metafy at $6 a month. Learn doesn't change that: browsing guides costs nothing in ManaLab.</p>
<h2>Try it</h2>
<p>Learn is part of ManaLab 3.0, along with the new look of the app. Download ManaLab free, play a few matches on Arena or Magic Online, and when a matchup keeps beating you, open Learn and start there.</p>
<p><a class="boton prim" href="/#descargar"><strong>Download ManaLab free →</strong></a></p>
<p class="antes">Before you start: <a href="/detailed-logs/">Detailed Logs</a> · <a href="/player-log/">Player.log</a> · <a href="/safety/">Is it safe?</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</main>
